Notebook[{
Cell["Diffusion Cartograms in the Wolfram Language", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"40383473-eb84-4407-8c65-18d0ffadf373"],

Cell["\<\
A self-contained pure-Wolfram implementation of the Gastner\[Dash]Newman \
density-equalising map algorithm.\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"5f6e4876-2c27-413a-888d-00ed970e3fa4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Marco Thiel, April 2026 \[LongDash] ",
 ButtonBox["github.com/mthiel74/Contiguous-Cartograms",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/mthiel74/Contiguous-Cartograms"], None}]
}], "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontSlant->Italic,ExpressionUUID->"045767d0-34e3-4e12-b471-e5efd71a4093"],

Cell["Abstract", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"64bdd57f-3ada-4538-9aaf-a00324ab3406"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Cartograms are maps in which the area of each region is deformed to be \
proportional to a statistical quantity \[LongDash] population, GDP, number of \
COVID cases, votes cast, and so on \[LongDash] while the topology (who is \
next to whom) is preserved. Gastner and Newman (2004) showed how to produce \
such maps by interpreting the quantity as a density and letting it diffuse to \
uniformity; every point of the map is advected by the resulting velocity \
field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["v",
     FontWeight->Bold], "=", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"\[Del]", "\[Rho]"}], "\[Rho]"]}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "26fa6c56-fef1-458f-ab0d-afaca304f22d"],
 ". This notebook presents a compact, pure-Wolfram-Language port of that \
algorithm. It ships as a paclet-style package ",
 StyleBox["CartogramWL", "Input"],
 " exposing both low-level primitives (",
 StyleBox["DiffusionSolver", "Input"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Cartogram", "Input"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["CartogramTransform", "Input"],
 ") and a one-liner ",
 StyleBox["WorldCartogram[metric]", "Input"],
 " that pulls country polygons and statistical values from the built-in ",
 StyleBox["CountryData", "Input"],
 " and returns a ready-to-publish figure. It supports any ",
 StyleBox["ColorData", "Input"],
 " gradient, a ",
 StyleBox["GeoBackground -> \"Satellite\"", "Input"],
 " mode that textures each country with deformed satellite imagery, \
user-supplied ",
 StyleBox["Association", "Input"],
 " input, visualisation of the underlying space deformation via a distortion \
grid, and a ",
 StyleBox["PerformanceGoal -> \"Speed\"", "Input"],
 " default that runs the full world pipeline in under a minute."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bcd1efb0-aae6-467f-9bfb-976cd6c839ca"],

