Cell["4.5 A detour: multi-part countries (Alaska, Hawaii)", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"a85bd2d4-728a-412f-a414-e652c5f0bcef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Wolfram's ",
 StyleBox["CountryData[\"UnitedStates\", \"Polygon\"]", "Input"],
 " only returns the contiguous 48 states. Alaska and Hawaii live under ",
 StyleBox["Entity[\"AdministrativeDivision\", {\"Alaska\", \
\"UnitedStates\"}]", "Input"],
 " and its Hawaii analogue. If we rasterised the bare ",
 StyleBox["CountryData", "Input"],
 " polygon the US would still grow on the cartogram \[LongDash] but only the \
lower 48 would grow, because Alaska and Hawaii would contribute zero density \
to the diffusion field and would not even appear on the map. ",
 StyleBox["CartogramWL", "Input"],
 " therefore splices the administrative-division polygons back in via a \
helper ",
 StyleBox["CountryPolygonRings[c]", "Input"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3941d9e6-e9f1-4bff-be4f-9a6a70359267"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"Length", " ", "@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"CountryPolygonRings", "[", "\"\<UnitedStates\>\"", "]"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"113", "  ", "--"}], " ", "28", " ", "mainland"}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{"77", " ", "Alaska", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"mainland", " ", "+", " ", "Aleutians"}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"8", " ", "Hawaii"}]}], " ", "*)"}]}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"f989fe57-a664-4b96-9739-cf281617bb7a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The figure below makes the effect unambiguous. We rasterise the world's GDP \
twice at identical cartogram parameters \[LongDash] once from the bare ",
 StyleBox["CountryData", "Input"],
 " polygons (left column), once from ",
 StyleBox["CountryPolygonRings", "Input"],
 " (right column) \[LongDash] and highlight just the United States in orange. \
Top row shows the geographic inputs; bottom row shows the GDP cartogram \
cropped to North America. Without the fix, Alaska and Hawaii are missing \
altogether; with the fix both show up on the geographic panel and both \
inflate alongside the mainland on the cartogram. The same hook can be used to \
splice in France's overseas departments, Portugal's Azores/Madeira, Denmark's \
Greenland, and so on."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"269fa45c-5c80-4522-bae1-95935c8c37fb"],

